  "title": "Example classification of the algorithm names used in the worked examples",
  "status": "illustrative",
  "$comment": "Facts about algorithms, not judgements: the family, the classical security strength in bits, and whether a cryptographically relevant quantum computer would break the algorithm. A policy refers to this set by its digest under classificationSource, and holds its own schedule or classes. The same facts can therefore serve several policies and several jurisdictions, and a correction is made once. The entries were moved here unchanged from the inline classification of policy-algorithm-transition 0.3, policy-edge-posture 0.2 and policy-readiness-gap 0.2, which held identical copies. Names follow the forms the examples use, including the CycloneDX cryptography registry form and some protocol code-point names; aligning these with the registry is open as cluster D of the decision backlog.",
